        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kremlin Arsenal, Moscow Kremlin, Cathedral Square, Russia, Moscow, Zelenograd\n- Buildings: Cathedral of the Archangel, Great Kremlin Palace, Ivan the Great Bell Tower, Saint Basil's Cathedral\n- Organizations: FC Zelenograd\n- Topics: architecture, geography, football\n\nFacts:\n- The Kremlin Arsenal was initially constructed in 1736 and has been rebuilt several times.\n- The Moscow Kremlin is a fortified complex in central Moscow overlooking the Moskva River to the south, Saint Basil's Cathedral and Red Square to the east, and the Alexander Garden to the west.\n- The Cathedral of the Archangel is located in Cathedral Square within the Moscow Kremlin in Russia, between the Great Kremlin Palace and the Ivan the Great Bell Tower.\n- FC Zelenograd is an association football club from Zelenograd, Moscow.",
